# Stela Flutter Engineering Standards

Follow `flutter-cursor-rules.md` at the repo root. Prefer these defaults unless extending an existing alternative already in the file you are editing.

## Preferred stack

| Concern | Package |
|---|---|
| State | `flutter_bloc` (Cubit/Bloc + sealed states) |
| DI | `get_it` + `injectable` |
| Local structured data | `isar` (or Isar Community) — not SharedPreferences |
| Secrets / tokens | `flutter_secure_storage` only |
| Serialization | `json_serializable` DTOs |
| Network | `dio` + `retrofit` |
| Images | `fast_cached_network_image` via `CachedImage` |
| Icons | `hugeicons` via `AppIcon` / `AppIcons` |
| Animations | `flutter_animate` |

## Architecture

```
presentation (widgets) → Cubit/Bloc → domain (use cases) → data (repos / retrofit / local)
```

- Widgets dispatch events / call cubit methods and render with `BlocBuilder` / `BlocSelector`. Never call repositories, Dio, Firestore, or secure storage from widgets.
- Cubits call use cases (or repositories via use cases). Never call Dio/Retrofit directly.
- Repositories own network and local persistence. Auth headers come from the Dio interceptor — do not pass `Bearer` tokens per call.
- Register dependencies in feature `di/` modules + root `configureDependencies()`. Prefer constructor injection into Cubits.

## State migration

- **New features / touched managers:** implement as Cubit/Bloc. Do not add new `ChangeNotifier` / `CustomProvider` classes.
- When editing an existing `*Provider`, migrate that manager to a Cubit in the same change when feasible.
- Name states with sealed classes / explicit fields — no loose booleans for multi-step flows.

## Networking & errors

- Map `DioException` to `AppFailure` subtypes before UI. UI never inspects status codes or `DioException`.
- Timeouts stay on the shared Dio client. Public endpoints (e.g. `/health`) must work without a token.
- Paginate list endpoints; use `ListView.builder` / `SliverList` for dynamic collections.

## Security & production

- Never store tokens in SharedPreferences, globals, or Isar.
- Never log tokens, passwords, or PII. No leftover `print()` in shipped paths.
- Guard double-submit on auth/payment/session actions.

## Icons & images

- Add icons to `AppIcons` and render with `AppIcon`. No raw Material `Icons.*` for app chrome.
- Network images only through `CachedImage`.
